<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khayr al-Nisa Begum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1579">1579</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Mahd-i Ulya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khayr al-Nisa Begum, known as Mahd-i Ulya, was a Safavid queen from the Mar'ashi family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mazandaran">Mazandaran</a>. As wife of Shah Mohammad Khodabanda she effectively ran the government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> after his accession in 1578, but her attempts to curb the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qizilbash">Qizilbash</a> chiefs led to her murder by them in 1579. She was the mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khayr-al-nisa-begum.jpg" alt="Khayr al-Nisa Begum" width="317" height="572" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 1584 artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Strangulation_of_Khayr_al-Nisa_Begum,_at_the_Safavid_court._Nusretname_(1584).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
